<title>INDIA: India forex reserves rise to $23.90 bln on Dec 6.</title>
<headline>India forex reserves rise to $23.90 bln on Dec 6.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-12-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's foreign exchange reserves rose to $23.90 billion on December 6, 1996, from $23.79 billion the previous week, the Reserve Bank of India said in its weekly statistical supplement on Saturday.</p>
<p>	 Foreign exchange reserves (in million U.S. dollars)</p>
<p>					   Dec 6	Nov 29	  Dec 8</p>
<p>					    1996	  1996	   1995</p>
<p>    Foreign currency assets     19,434	19,388	 17,283</p>
<p>    Gold				 4,347	 4,382	  4,429</p>
<p>    SDRs				   125	    17	     18</p>
<p>    Total			     23,906	23,787	 21,730</p>
<p>.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
